      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The traditional board often defaults to an archetype that favors a certain look—think polished, traditionally Westernized presentation, often leaning toward established Anglo-American or European business styles. They tend to equate \"gravitas\" with a specific, often homogenous, presentation of power. While diversity is the modern goal, the *archetype* they are subconsciously looking for usually aligns with established, familiar markers of old-money corporate success.",
